    1 """The honest-churn arm (docs/revision/churn/churn-plan.md, draft 1): the nine honest opponents also retire their identity
    2 and re-enter under a fresh one with probability p per round, so the newest identity no longer marks the deviating
    3 provider. D2+H3 attacks against R3 (F111), C* and B3 (F000) on the six fresh markets at rho 0.2, for each churn rate,
    4 searched, evaluated and doubled with the frozen stage functions of scripts/revision_v2.py.
    5 
    6 The frozen code is not edited (code freeze 627a2de). Churn enters through `Cell.others`: `install()` wraps
    7 `revision_v2.train_cell`, which `eval_cell` also calls, so every stage that builds a cell for a churn job (search, twin
    8 search, reference menu in the doubling diagnostic, evaluation) runs with churning opponents. Process pools install the
    9 wrapper in their initialiser. A churn decision is drawn from the episode's per-round, per-entity policy seed, so it is
   10 deterministic and identical across the three rules on the same seed.
   11 
   12 Churn job ids carry the suffix `|churn<p>`, so they never collide with the registered D2+H3 records that the frozen
   13 reference menus read. The frozen truthful reference of each (market, rule) is reused, not reselected, and every
   14 reference episode runs under the same churn (see the plan, section 3). Each churn rate writes to its own directory."""
   15 from __future__ import annotations
   16 
   17 import argparse
   18 import json
   19 import sys
   20 from concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor
   21 from pathlib import Path
